    "answer": {
      "short": "Refund of \\$751.60.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Taxable income} &= (29760 + 2500) - 1090 \\\\\n\\text{Taxable income} &= \\$31170\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe taxable income is in the \\$18,201–\\$45,000 bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Excess} &= 31170 - 18200 \\\\\n\\text{Excess} &= \\$12970 \\\\\n\\text{Tax payable} &= 0 + 0.19 \\times 12970 \\\\\n\\text{Tax payable} &= \\$2464.30 \\\\\n\\text{Instalments} - \\text{Tax payable} &= 3215.90 - 2464.30 \\\\\n\\text{Instalments} - \\text{Tax payable} &= \\$751.60\n\\end{align*}$$\nHe has paid too much tax, so he receives a refund of \\$751.60.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
